A||||7||Kage86GT4SP||My clutch pedal is getting lower and lower....||||1
Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||11-10-1999||02:12 AM||||Hi all...<P>I have an 86 SE V6, 4spd.  145K<P>I am having to push the clutch pedal almost to the floor to shift, particularly into reverse.  It is getting noticeably worse.<P>The fluid level looks fine, and when I push the clutch in, it stays in... but man, it's a long way to the floor.<P>Pedal height and feel remains the same.<P>In order, what steps should I take to fix this?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||sinoloa||11-10-1999||02:36 AM||||It sounds like you need to replace the clutch, pressure plate, and pilot bearing (the throw-out bearing).  Its recommended that you change both the clutch and the pressure plate at the same time.  Fluid clutches are kind of weird.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||11-10-1999||05:53 AM||||<BR>Don't be too quick to rule out the hydraulic system.<P>If you don't know <B>THE</B> thread to read at this forum about clutches, you must be new here. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||DJRice||11-10-1999||10:07 AM||||Make sure you are well rested before you head to "the thread".  Also have some kind of food and drink on hand, because you will be busy for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||11-10-1999||10:10 AM||||I'd bet you a Big Mac your clutch master cylinder is bad.  (But if it's been driven that way for a long time, the throwout bearing and pressure plate might be forked up, too.)  Here's hoping you get away with $90 and a couple hours' work.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan||11-10-1999||10:47 AM|||| Before you tear it down, check for a bent clutch petal.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||11-10-1999||11:25 AM||||Dan people seem to forget that the pedal gets bent and to change it with a steel one.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ditz88GT||11-10-1999||12:13 PM||||I had a problem kinda like that.  The arm on the side of the trans was slowly bending and cracking (The arm that the hydraulic cylinder presses to release the clutch).  It also was shaving of the pin that held it in place.  I just had it welded and that fixed it, but I had already ran out and bought the whole clutch kit.  The first symptom was when I would sit with the car running, in gear and clutch depressed, it would slowly creep out.||||reg||1
